SUMMARY:MAM Free First Thursday - Analog Night
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy free general admission to the Museum\, activities\, food trucks\, a cash bar\, and so much more! This party is made possible by the generous support of TD Bank.\nSlow down\, unwind\, and take a break from screens for an Analog Night of creativity\, fun\, and community! \nPROGRAM\nMAM Family Learning Lab\nVisit the Family Learning Lab on the 3rd Floor | 5:30–8:30 p.m. \nArt Activity: Story Cubes Game\nLearn how to design cubes printed with pictures\, icons\, or words to spark imagination and create spontaneous stories. Open to all ages. \nDJ April of Eighty-Six’d the Magazine\nLeir Hall | 5–9 p.m.\nDJ April will be spinning vinyl all night!\nEighty-Six’d is a Montclair-based monthly print magazine covering art\, food\, & culture in Essex County. \nThe Player Agency\nLeir Hall | 5–9 p.m.\nConnect with family and friends by learning how to play games with The Player Agency board game shop. \nMAM welcome and Introductions\nLeir Hall | 5:30 p.m. \nMontclair Public Library\nLeir Hall | 5:30–8:30 p.m.\nRegister for a library card and learn about all the resources available at the library! \nEast Side Mags Table\nLeir Hall | 5:30–8:30 p.m.\nLearn about our local comic store\, East Side Mags\, and all they offer. \nEast Side Mags—Kids Dungeons and Dragons one shot\nStudio A | 6–7 p.m.\nDungeons and Dragons one shot\, open to kids ages 9 and up\nLearn more about the campaign HERE: DND One shot-Night of the Catastrophic Curiosities ↗\n10 first come first serve slots available. Registration to join the campaign will be open soon! \nDocent Gallery Tour\nMeet at Cornerstone Café | 6:30 p.m.\nEnjoy a guided tour of Nadia Myre: Analog/ues. \nMSU Cali Collective solos\nMeet in Lehman Court | 7–7:30 p.m.\nMembers of the Cali Collective Ensemble will perform solos inspired by an artwork on view. \nEast Side Mags—Adult Dungeons and Dragons one shot\nStudio A | 7:30–8:30 p.m.\nDungeons and Dragons one shot\, open to ages 18+\nLearn more about the campaign HERE: DND One shot-Night of the Catastrophic Curiosities ↗\n10 first come first serve slots available. Registration to join the campaign will be open soon! \nDocent Gallery Tour\nMeet at Cornerstone Café | 7:30 p.m.\nEnjoy a guided tour of Shifting Terrain: Perspectives on Land in North America. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/mam-free-first-thursday-analog-night/
